## Source arithmetic and warning custody

The first outer/inner loops retain caller pointer order and left-to-right
`ZoneArea(i) += A(j)`. Self and floor-floor pairs are excluded; floors otherwise
see every selected class. Other pairs require strict azimuth difference >10
and <350, or strict tilt difference >10. No modulo-angle conversion is added.
After each source row, `ZoneArea(i) <= 0.0` appends one typed warning record.
The source warning call followed by its surface/zone continuation is represented
by that record, using the actual input identities and names. Relative record
order is retained; global diagnostic indexes/backend delivery remain unowned.
The literal warning head is `CalcApproximateViewFactors: Zero area for all other
zone surfaces.`; its continuation is `Happens for Surface="..." in Zone=...`.

Only after all area/warning rows, F is initialized to positive zero. The second
outer/inner loops repeat visibility and assign `F(j,i) = A(j)/ZoneArea(i)` only
when `ZoneArea(i) > 0.0`. Flat storage is row-first, offset j*N+i with zero-based
Rust indices, matching the actual Objexx Array2 index. The output retains both
ZoneArea and F, unchanged context and input ID order, plus warning records.

The deliberate numerical delta to the old Rust kernel is removal of its
`<= f64::EPSILON` outer skip in favor of the exact source >0 inner guard.
Positive tiny seen areas are divided; nonpositive areas leave zero F. IEEE
comparisons and arithmetic are otherwise unchecked as in the selected source:
no finite guard, output clamp, reciprocity correction or fallback is introduced.
The shared legacy adapter copies only class/area/angles and discards the typed
warning-index ledger because that existing interface owns no IDs/names/backend.
It does not fabricate those metadata fields for the new API.

## Seven proposed, unexecuted tests

1. Asymmetric areas: actual input ID order, ZoneArea, directed F(j,i) offsets,
   nonzero entries and positive-zero diagonal.
2. Exact 10/350-degree and adjacent angle boundaries, tilt-only visibility,
   and 360-degree difference without normalization.
3. Floor-floor exclusion and same-orientation floor-roof visibility.
4. Positive area below epsilon, with exact shared-kernel legacy/public equality.
5. Zero/negative diagnostic areas: zero F and warning identity/name/order.
6. Positive-area floating-point accumulation demonstrates caller order matters.
7. Zone/duplicate association failures plus the direct empty helper boundary.

These are literal-input source regression tests, not Native-generated expected
answers or executed scientific comparisons. Negative/empty diagnostic cases do
not expand CON production scope. No test, compiler, formatter, project import,
engine, binary, weather payload or scientific result was executed/read here.

